# mr_vmu_rt1176 copter under Renode.
#
# The CubeOrange copter mission, on the other Zephyr board. Everything the two
# flights share is identical - frame, loop rate, gains, waypoint speed, the
# INS/compass offsets that keep the emulated sensors from reading exactly zero -
# so that a difference between the two flights is a difference between the
# boards and not between their parameter files.
#
# What is board specific:
#   BRD_IO_ENABLE  absent: this board has no IOMCU, so the motors come out of
#                  the FMU FlexPWM channels and there is nothing to enable.
#   COMPASS_*      the emulated compass is an IST8310 on the external bus
#                  (see Tools/renode/platforms/imxrt1176_base.repl), found by
#                  ArduPilot's own probing rather than by a hwdef line.
#   SERIAL1/3      SERIAL_ORDER on this board is OTG1 USART4 USART8 USART3 ...,
#                  so SERIAL1 is lpuart4 (the flight's MAVLink link, which the
#                  harness attaches a socket to) and SERIAL3 is lpuart3 (GPS).
#                  Both already have the protocols this file sets.
# Shared by BOTH CubeOrange copter flights - the Zephyr one and the ChibiOS
# reference it is read against. They must fly byte-identical parameters or a
# difference in where they land says nothing about the HALs.
#
# The ChibiOS reference used to fly KakuteF4-copter.parm, which differed here
# only in leaving BRD_IO_ENABLE alone. That one line moved its motors onto the
# AP_IOMCU model while the Zephyr flight drove the FMU timers, so the two runs
# were not using the same actuator path and "ChibiOS lands inside 3 m" did not
# cover the path the Zephyr flight actually uses.
#
# Renode supplies the flight state and attached sensors rather than physical
# RC, safety-switch, power-monitor and peripheral wiring.
ARMING_CHECK 0
AHRS_EKF_TYPE 3
BATT_MONITOR 0
BRD_SAFETY_DEFLT 0
FS_THR_ENABLE 0
RC_PROTOCOLS 0
GPS1_TYPE 1
SERIAL3_PROTOCOL 5
# Keep telemetry below the UART's buffer capacity.
SR1_EXT_STAT 2
SR1_POSITION 2
SR1_EXTRA1 2
SR1_EXTRA2 2
AUTO_OPTIONS 3
# Match the Betaflight motor order the bfx physics model expects.
FRAME_CLASS 1
FRAME_TYPE 12
# Match the controller timing to the cadence Renode can sustain.
SCHED_LOOP_RATE 125
# Keep the compact mission inside conservative acceleration and speed limits.
WP_SPD 1
WP_ACC 0.5
WP_YAW_BEHAVIOR 0
# Standard SITL multicopter tune and calibrated accelerometer values.
ATC_ANG_RLL_P 2
ATC_ANG_PIT_P 2
ATC_RAT_RLL_P 0.05
ATC_RAT_RLL_I 0.05
ATC_RAT_RLL_D 0.001
ATC_RAT_PIT_P 0.05
ATC_RAT_PIT_I 0.05
ATC_RAT_PIT_D 0.001
ATC_RAT_YAW_P 0.3
ATC_RAT_YAW_I 0.02
MOT_THST_EXPO 0.65
MOT_THST_HOVER 0.39
MOT_BAT_VOLT_MIN 9.6
MOT_BAT_VOLT_MAX 12.8
INS_ACCOFFS_X 0.001
INS_ACCOFFS_Y 0.001
INS_ACCOFFS_Z 0.001
INS_ACCSCAL_X 1.001
INS_ACCSCAL_Y 1.001
INS_ACCSCAL_Z 1.001
INS_GYR_CAL 0
LAND_DISARMDELAY 1

# --- CubeOrangeZephyr additions -------------------------------------------
# AP_HAL_Zephyr can build IOMCU support but the 1.5Mbaud link does not carry
# data yet, so the motors come out of the FMU timers. The Renode platform is
# re-pointed to match by cube_orange_zephyr_actuators.repl.

# Emulation runs at a fraction of real time, so board-seconds are expensive.
# These trim the phases that carry no verdict (2026-09-12 timeline: 53 s
# pre-arm, 52 s mission, ~30 s land + disarm at 1/9.5 real time):
#   EK3_GPS_CHECK 0    - the EKF used GPS 28 s after the 3D fix while its
#                        drift/speed pre-flight checks settled; the emulated
#                        GPS has no drift to check.
#   LAND_SPEED 100     - descend the final 10 m at 1 m/s instead of 0.5 m/s.
EK3_GPS_CHECK 0
LAND_SPEED 100
